  #block[
    *Read the following passage carefully, then answer questions 45–50.*

    An earthquake is the sudden shaking of the ground caused by the movement of rocks deep inside the Earth. The most powerful shaking usually lasts only seconds, yet it can damage or knock down buildings. During an earthquake, experts advise you to drop to the ground, take cover under a strong table, and hold on until the shaking stops. After the shaking ends, leave the building carefully and move to an open area, away from walls and power lines.
  ]

